# Copy this file to .env.e2e.local (already gitignored via ".env*" in
# .gitignore — never commit real values) and fill in real values.
#
# Purpose: this app's own .env.local now holds Clerk PRODUCTION keys (see
# CLAUDE.md history) — correct for `npm run dev` day-to-day, but wrong for
# the local Playwright/Audit E2E suite, which needs to drive a real
# Clerk sign-in from a script running on localhost. Clerk Production
# instances categorically refuse any browser-side auth operation whose
# Origin isn't the verified production domain ("Production Keys are only
# allowed for domain ...") — that's a Clerk security feature, not a bug,
# and must stay that way. Development-instance keys don't have that
# restriction, so E2E auth needs its own, separate set of keys — this file.
#
# e2e/auth-setup.mjs loads this file (if present) BEFORE .env.local and
# lets these values win, so the E2E suite always authenticates against the
# Development instance regardless of what .env.local is currently set to.
# It also hard-refuses to run if the resolved CLERK_SECRET_KEY starts with
# "sk_live_" — this file existing and being correct is what makes E2E work
# locally at all now; see e2e/README.md for exactly where to get these two
# values from (a Development instance already exists and is already used
# by this project's Vercel Preview environment — no new Clerk instance
# needs to be created).
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="pk_test_xxxxxxxx"
CLERK_SECRET_KEY="sk_test_xxxxxxxx"

# Same DB overrides e2e/README.md has always documented as manual
# `npm run dev` env-var prefixes — consolidated here so one `source
# .env.e2e.local` covers everything the E2E dev server needs, Clerk
# included. See e2e/README.md for what each value must point to and why.
DATABASE_URL=""
AUDIT_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:localtest@localhost:5433/public_map_audit_test"
